1
00:01:00,945 --> 00:01:04,745
What you did today was totally inhumane.

2
00:01:04,825 --> 00:01:07,505
In that case, I have nothing to lose now.

3
00:01:07,585 --> 00:01:08,545
I see you've made your choice.

4
00:01:09,905 --> 00:01:11,065
Why wouldn't you sue her?

5
00:01:11,145 --> 00:01:15,145
I don't want to make her choose between
justice and being a good daughter.

6
00:01:15,225 --> 00:01:17,585
-You're fired, Utt.
-You will regret this.

7
00:01:17,665 --> 00:01:18,745
Runch.

8
00:01:19,745 --> 00:01:20,745
I want a divorce.

9
00:01:20,825 --> 00:01:24,345
I don't want my love
to keep hurting you anymore.

10
00:01:24,985 --> 00:01:27,305
I'll give your mother what she wants.

11
00:01:27,905 --> 00:01:30,425
You can go back to being her daughter now.

12
00:01:30,505 --> 00:01:32,585
-Make yourself at home.
-Thank you.

13
00:01:37,825 --> 00:01:39,385
Is Runch still asleep?

14
00:01:39,985 --> 00:01:42,945
She's at her house.
Why would she sleep here?

15
00:01:43,465 --> 00:01:44,945
What? She didn't come back here?

16
00:01:45,905 --> 00:01:47,065
What do you mean?

17
00:01:48,105 --> 00:01:50,465
There's a rumor going around.

18
00:01:51,065 --> 00:01:52,185
Saying what?

19
00:01:52,265 --> 00:01:55,305
That Runch and Neen got divorced.

20
00:02:06,345 --> 00:02:09,905
Come on, Runch. Why aren't you picking up?

21
00:02:15,905 --> 00:02:17,385
What on earth is she doing?

22
00:02:17,945 --> 00:02:19,945
Come on. Pick up.

23
00:02:33,105 --> 00:02:35,745
Excuse me. Is Runchlaphat at work?

24
00:02:35,825 --> 00:02:37,625
This is her mother speaking.

25
00:02:52,785 --> 00:02:56,225
Why didn't you tell me
you already divorced that bitch?

26
00:02:59,505 --> 00:03:01,705
Can you talk about her nicely for once?

27
00:03:01,785 --> 00:03:03,905
Why should I?

28
00:03:03,985 --> 00:03:05,785
She's the one who made you sad.

29
00:03:09,585 --> 00:03:12,465
She's not the one who made me sad.

30
00:03:13,705 --> 00:03:14,865
You are.

31
00:03:20,425 --> 00:03:21,985
You caused all this.

32
00:03:23,665 --> 00:03:26,985
You drove the one I love the most
to leave me.

33
00:03:27,065 --> 00:03:28,585
Don't blame me.

34
00:03:29,105 --> 00:03:32,505
I did it all for your sake.

35
00:03:34,465 --> 00:03:36,945
I've put up with so much

36
00:03:37,025 --> 00:03:39,065
and made sacrifices my whole life.

37
00:03:39,665 --> 00:03:41,505
You think this is what I wanted?

38
00:03:42,705 --> 00:03:45,585
For my daughter to stand here blaming me?

39
00:03:45,665 --> 00:03:47,705
I'm not blaming you, Mom.

40
00:03:49,225 --> 00:03:50,785
I'm just telling the truth.

41
00:03:50,865 --> 00:03:54,465
Whose truth? Her truth?

42
00:03:55,625 --> 00:03:58,585
That woman who tore our family apart?!

43
00:03:58,665 --> 00:04:00,985
Neen didn't tear our family apart.

44
00:04:02,185 --> 00:04:05,825
You never accepted that I've grown up.
That's what tore us apart.

45
00:04:06,625 --> 00:04:08,625
I want a life of my own.

46
00:04:09,145 --> 00:04:10,905
A life of your own?

47
00:04:12,065 --> 00:04:14,265
By letting that girl into your life

48
00:04:14,345 --> 00:04:16,705
so she can humiliate me
in front of everyone?

49
00:04:16,785 --> 00:04:20,745
Neen wasn't the one who humiliated you.

50
00:04:21,905 --> 00:04:24,265
It's your own actions that did it.

51
00:04:25,545 --> 00:04:28,425
I'm your mother,
the one who gave birth to you

52
00:04:28,945 --> 00:04:30,665
and raised you.

53
00:04:31,265 --> 00:04:32,225
And today,

54
00:04:32,305 --> 00:04:34,945
you're saying everything was my fault?

55
00:04:35,025 --> 00:04:36,945
That's not what I said.

56
00:04:38,505 --> 00:04:40,625
I'm saying you're the only one

57
00:04:42,905 --> 00:04:45,385
who made me lose the one I love the most.

58
00:04:47,825 --> 00:04:51,505
If losing her hurts you that much…

59
00:04:56,625 --> 00:04:58,945
how do you think I felt

60
00:05:00,985 --> 00:05:02,625
when I lost you?

61
00:05:08,345 --> 00:05:09,945
You never lost me.

62
00:05:15,185 --> 00:05:16,865
You're still my mother,

63
00:05:17,825 --> 00:05:19,665
and I'm still your daughter.

64
00:05:24,385 --> 00:05:27,345
You just need to stop
trying to control my life.

65
00:05:28,305 --> 00:05:29,665
You want me to stop

66
00:05:30,345 --> 00:05:32,705
and just watch your life fall apart?

67
00:05:32,785 --> 00:05:35,705
My life isn't falling apart
because of Neen.

68
00:05:38,825 --> 00:05:42,465
It fell apart
because you never supported me.

69
00:05:44,345 --> 00:05:45,705
How ungrateful.

70
00:05:46,665 --> 00:05:48,665
What an ungrateful child you are.

71
00:05:50,505 --> 00:05:53,345
That bitch really changed you, huh?

72
00:05:54,665 --> 00:05:56,465
If I had known,

73
00:05:56,545 --> 00:05:58,705
I would've kept slapping her that day

74
00:05:58,785 --> 00:06:01,305
-until I ruined her face!
-Mom!

75
00:06:03,345 --> 00:06:05,865
There's just no fixing you, is there?

76
00:06:06,385 --> 00:06:08,985
Why would you go around
attacking people for no reason?

77
00:06:09,065 --> 00:06:10,105
Runch…

78
00:06:15,105 --> 00:06:17,025
If you keep acting this way,

79
00:06:17,825 --> 00:06:20,425
you won't get a single dime from me.

80
00:06:21,225 --> 00:06:22,545
And we'll go our separate ways.

81
00:06:25,065 --> 00:06:28,225
I don't even want to know
if you're sick or on your deathbed.

82
00:06:28,305 --> 00:06:30,065
I'm your mother.

83
00:06:30,865 --> 00:06:31,985
How dare you?

84
00:06:34,345 --> 00:06:36,745
How could you say that
when I gave birth to you,

85
00:06:37,345 --> 00:06:40,345
when I've dedicated my life to you
all this time?

86
00:06:46,785 --> 00:06:49,025
I know you've dedicated your life to me,

87
00:06:49,625 --> 00:06:51,785
and I've been trying to defend you.

88
00:06:53,745 --> 00:06:55,585
You only got away with what you did

89
00:06:56,545 --> 00:06:58,425
because Neen respects me.

90
00:07:00,985 --> 00:07:02,665
But from now on,

91
00:07:04,225 --> 00:07:06,105
if you do something to her again,

92
00:07:08,905 --> 00:07:11,705
I can't guarantee your safety.

93
00:07:11,785 --> 00:07:12,905
Runch.

94
00:07:14,505 --> 00:07:17,065
Will you really let her harass me?

95
00:07:22,865 --> 00:07:23,785
Mom.

96
00:07:27,905 --> 00:07:29,465
Think about it.

97
00:07:30,465 --> 00:07:32,305
Who's harassing who?

98
00:07:41,305 --> 00:07:42,625
You should leave.

99
00:07:44,185 --> 00:07:45,825
And don't come back again.

100
00:07:46,345 --> 00:07:48,105
I want to be alone.

101
00:07:48,185 --> 00:07:49,265
Runch…

102
00:07:49,945 --> 00:07:51,785
Runch, Runch!

103
00:07:51,865 --> 00:07:54,545
Runch, let's talk this out. Runch!

104
00:07:55,225 --> 00:07:56,425
Runch!

105
00:07:56,945 --> 00:07:58,345
Runch.

106
00:08:15,865 --> 00:08:17,585
Easy now.

107
00:08:17,665 --> 00:08:20,665
At this rate, you won't
be able to go home by yourself.

108
00:08:20,745 --> 00:08:23,945
Then you'll just have to drive me.
That's all. No big deal.

109
00:08:24,025 --> 00:08:27,025
-Neen, this isn't funny.
-Yeah.

110
00:08:27,105 --> 00:08:29,505
Enough. Enough, Neen!

111
00:08:30,705 --> 00:08:31,785
What the heck?

112
00:08:31,865 --> 00:08:33,505
Are you drinking yourself to death?

113
00:08:33,585 --> 00:08:35,425
I'm not gonna die.

114
00:08:37,664 --> 00:08:39,065
I'm just hurt.

115
00:08:40,784 --> 00:08:42,585
I really don't get you.

116
00:08:42,664 --> 00:08:46,225
If you still love Runch that much,
why divorce her?

117
00:08:46,785 --> 00:08:49,945
Because she always made sacrifices for me.

118
00:08:52,945 --> 00:08:55,025
Ever since she married me,

119
00:08:55,745 --> 00:08:58,585
she never got to be happy for real.

120
00:08:58,665 --> 00:09:01,225
She always had to defend me, get hurt,

121
00:09:01,305 --> 00:09:03,185
and choose between me and her mother.

122
00:09:03,265 --> 00:09:04,105
Neen.

123
00:09:04,185 --> 00:09:08,025
None of that was your fault.
You didn't ask for her to be hurt for you.

124
00:09:08,105 --> 00:09:09,985
No, no. Still, I was…

125
00:09:10,065 --> 00:09:13,025
I was the one who caused it.
I'm the reason.

126
00:09:14,825 --> 00:09:18,305
If me being by her side
means she has to suffer,

127
00:09:18,385 --> 00:09:20,905
then it's only natural
I wouldn't want to stay.

128
00:09:21,425 --> 00:09:24,745
I want her to be happy for real.

129
00:09:24,825 --> 00:09:28,265
The kind of happiness that doesn't
come at the cost of being hurt

130
00:09:28,345 --> 00:09:30,345
or being called an ungrateful child.

131
00:09:34,345 --> 00:09:36,105
-Aw. It's okay.
-Come on, Neen.

132
00:09:36,185 --> 00:09:39,345
You need to be kinder to yourself.

133
00:09:43,025 --> 00:09:45,985
When love comes
at the cost of sacrificing yourself,

134
00:09:46,065 --> 00:09:47,785
it can hurt like hell.

135
00:09:56,945 --> 00:09:58,225
What should we do now?

136
00:10:03,265 --> 00:10:04,425
<i>Hey, guys.</i>

137
00:10:04,505 --> 00:10:07,545
<i>Today I'm showing you a product</i>
<i>that I really love.</i>

138
00:10:07,625 --> 00:10:12,025
<i>Here it is. A smooth underarm cream!</i>

139
00:10:12,105 --> 00:10:14,625
<i>Make sure to hit that button</i>
<i>before it runs out.</i>

140
00:10:14,705 --> 00:10:15,705
PJW GLOW CREAM - 590 BAHT

141
00:10:15,785 --> 00:10:16,825
DOES IT ABSORB QUICKLY?

142
00:10:16,905 --> 00:10:17,865
I USED IT AND REALLY LIKED IT.
TOTALLY NON-GREASY.

143
00:10:17,945 --> 00:10:18,945
I BOUGHT IT MANY TIMES.

144
00:10:19,025 --> 00:10:19,945
NEEN'S MOM

145
00:10:20,025 --> 00:10:22,545
Hello, Pin. Are you with Neen?

146
00:10:24,585 --> 00:10:25,785
Did something happen?

147
00:10:25,865 --> 00:10:29,585
She isn't home yet,
and I can't reach her at all.

148
00:10:30,225 --> 00:10:33,785
Please don't panic.
I'll try calling her for you.

149
00:10:34,545 --> 00:10:37,265
Okay. Thank you so much.
Please do that for me.

150
00:10:37,345 --> 00:10:39,585
I'm worried she'll act on her own again.

151
00:10:41,065 --> 00:10:43,905
Got it. I'll go see her.

152
00:10:43,985 --> 00:10:45,625
Please don't worry.

153
00:10:58,105 --> 00:10:59,145
Yes, Pin?

154
00:11:00,665 --> 00:11:03,825
Runch. Is Neen with you right now?

155
00:11:04,945 --> 00:11:08,545
No, she isn't. Did something happen?

156
00:11:08,625 --> 00:11:10,585
<i>Well, Neen's mother called me.</i>

157
00:11:10,665 --> 00:11:13,785
She said Neen isn't home yet,
and she can't reach her at all.

158
00:11:13,865 --> 00:11:15,745
Not at all, you say?

159
00:11:15,825 --> 00:11:16,665
<i>No.</i>

160
00:11:17,185 --> 00:11:18,985
Then I'll help find her too.

161
00:11:19,065 --> 00:11:22,065
If someone finds her,
please call me right away.

162
00:11:57,985 --> 00:12:01,025
<i>Sometimes disappearing</i>

163
00:12:01,105 --> 00:12:03,665
<i>is the only way for the one you love</i>

164
00:12:03,745 --> 00:12:05,465
<i>to be truly happy.</i>

165
00:12:06,065 --> 00:12:08,425
INSTAGRAM - YOUR STORY

166
00:12:20,065 --> 00:12:23,665
SOMETIMES DISAPPEARING IS THE ONLY WAY
FOR THE ONE YOU LOVE TO BE TRULY HAPPY

167
00:12:43,345 --> 00:12:44,305
It was just a fight.

168
00:12:45,345 --> 00:12:46,505
We'll make up soon.

169
00:12:48,465 --> 00:12:51,305
Don't worry about it. Don't worry.

170
00:12:51,385 --> 00:12:53,905
I'm her mother. How could I be wrong?

171
00:12:59,865 --> 00:13:02,825
I never meant for it to turn out this way!

172
00:13:07,105 --> 00:13:09,625
It's all your fault. Your fault!

173
00:13:10,145 --> 00:13:13,225
It's all your fault, Peeracha.

174
00:13:27,345 --> 00:13:28,305
Peeracha…

175
00:13:41,345 --> 00:13:42,985
<i>You know…</i>

176
00:13:43,065 --> 00:13:46,025
<i>Ever since the day I decided</i>
<i>to love a woman,</i>

177
00:13:46,105 --> 00:13:48,665
I've known my life wouldn't be easy.

178
00:13:49,745 --> 00:13:51,505
And if it weren't for you,

179
00:13:52,665 --> 00:13:54,905
I wouldn't want to keep moving on.

180
00:14:01,065 --> 00:14:03,505
<i>I may not be a perfect woman.</i>

181
00:14:03,585 --> 00:14:05,265
I have responsibilities.

182
00:14:05,945 --> 00:14:07,585
I have my own world,

183
00:14:08,385 --> 00:14:09,905
which can feel heavy at times.

184
00:14:10,625 --> 00:14:12,345
But if you accept,

185
00:14:12,425 --> 00:14:15,385
I want you to be there
by my side, in my world,

186
00:14:15,465 --> 00:14:16,665
on every good day

187
00:14:16,745 --> 00:14:19,105
<i>and every difficult day.</i>

188
00:14:19,185 --> 00:14:22,545
<i>Will you marry me? Will you be my wife</i>

189
00:14:23,265 --> 00:14:24,985
and my family?

190
00:14:38,345 --> 00:14:39,345
Neen.

191
00:14:40,105 --> 00:14:41,105
Neen!

192
00:14:52,385 --> 00:14:53,385
Neen!

193
00:14:53,465 --> 00:14:54,545
Neen!

194
00:14:54,625 --> 00:14:56,105
Neen!

195
00:15:07,225 --> 00:15:08,625
Neen!

196
00:15:09,385 --> 00:15:10,625
Neen!

197
00:15:11,145 --> 00:15:13,865
Neen! Neen!

198
00:15:13,945 --> 00:15:16,425
Neen! Neen…

199
00:15:16,945 --> 00:15:17,785
Runch!

200
00:15:23,545 --> 00:15:24,585
What, Runch?

201
00:15:29,345 --> 00:15:30,785
What are you doing?

202
00:15:30,865 --> 00:15:33,265
Why would you do this?
Why are you hurting yourself?

203
00:15:33,345 --> 00:15:36,585
What are you talking about?
I'm not hurting myself.

204
00:15:40,105 --> 00:15:41,225
I just…

205
00:15:44,665 --> 00:15:45,865
I just

206
00:15:45,945 --> 00:15:49,305
wanted to be in the water where it's quiet

207
00:15:51,185 --> 00:15:53,105
so my heart could take a break.

208
00:15:56,345 --> 00:15:58,705
I want to forget everything
for a little while,

209
00:15:58,785 --> 00:16:00,985
at least just to quiet my mind.

210
00:16:31,105 --> 00:16:32,105
Runch.

211
00:16:36,985 --> 00:16:38,465
Can I ask you something?

212
00:16:47,425 --> 00:16:49,065
If you could go back in time,

213
00:16:51,105 --> 00:16:52,825
would you still marry me?

214
00:16:56,425 --> 00:16:57,745
Of course I would.

215
00:16:58,945 --> 00:17:01,225
I'd do it no matter what.

216
00:17:02,065 --> 00:17:03,745
Every time I have to choose,

217
00:17:04,865 --> 00:17:07,265
I'd still choose you to be my wife.

218
00:17:12,585 --> 00:17:13,625
Then…

219
00:17:17,265 --> 00:17:18,704
I guess I regret nothing

220
00:17:19,424 --> 00:17:21,704
about how we once chose each other.

221
00:17:32,225 --> 00:17:33,425
Thank you

222
00:17:35,385 --> 00:17:37,105
for loving me this much.

223
00:17:41,385 --> 00:17:44,505
I was always happy
when I was with you, Runch.

224
00:17:49,985 --> 00:17:52,145
I'll love you forever, Neen.

225
00:18:26,865 --> 00:18:28,425
I just don't get it.

226
00:18:28,505 --> 00:18:30,825
Everywhere I apply, they won't hire me.

227
00:18:32,905 --> 00:18:34,385
You really don't know?

228
00:18:34,985 --> 00:18:36,265
Know what?

229
00:18:37,305 --> 00:18:39,185
Remember who you messed with?

230
00:18:42,345 --> 00:18:45,905
Ms. Peeracha is
Chairman Thanachai's daughter.

231
00:18:45,985 --> 00:18:48,905
That family has strong connections
across industries.

232
00:18:49,625 --> 00:18:52,425
Did you really think what you did
would stay in the company?

233
00:18:52,505 --> 00:18:53,985
So what?

234
00:18:54,625 --> 00:18:56,065
Are you saying I got banned?

235
00:18:56,145 --> 00:18:58,025
Not just banned.

236
00:18:58,105 --> 00:19:00,545
Your career is basically over.

237
00:19:00,625 --> 00:19:02,305
You messed with the wrong person.

238
00:19:02,385 --> 00:19:03,945
When you mess with powerful people,

239
00:19:04,025 --> 00:19:05,985
they can get you blacklisted
just like that.

240
00:19:06,065 --> 00:19:08,145
I didn't do anything wrong!

241
00:19:11,145 --> 00:19:12,225
Damn it.

242
00:19:13,625 --> 00:19:16,225
I'm not letting
those two women ruin my life.

243
00:19:20,425 --> 00:19:22,665
BOSS'S MOTHER

244
00:19:27,105 --> 00:19:28,265
Look at you.

245
00:19:29,385 --> 00:19:31,705
I can't help but feel bad for you.

246
00:19:33,225 --> 00:19:37,185
I'm sorry you got fired.

247
00:19:39,185 --> 00:19:41,225
I know who was behind it.

248
00:19:43,505 --> 00:19:44,545
It's so unfair.

249
00:19:44,625 --> 00:19:46,625
Abusing her power

250
00:19:46,705 --> 00:19:50,385
by ruining someone's life
just for her own satisfaction.

251
00:19:51,665 --> 00:19:53,305
I'm having a really hard time.

252
00:19:54,385 --> 00:19:56,065
Everywhere I go, they won't hire me.

253
00:19:57,745 --> 00:19:58,985
I don't know what to do.

254
00:20:00,065 --> 00:20:03,545
I have to pay off my debts,
my car loan, and my mortgage.

255
00:20:06,585 --> 00:20:09,665
Hey, I understand.

256
00:20:10,945 --> 00:20:13,105
This should never happen
to someone like you.

257
00:20:14,705 --> 00:20:16,825
I know a way you can earn money.

258
00:20:19,585 --> 00:20:22,985
The question is, would you dare to do it?

259
00:20:26,305 --> 00:20:27,745
What do you mean?

260
00:21:33,545 --> 00:21:36,385
Is there anything else I can do for you?

261
00:21:37,385 --> 00:21:39,865
That should be all. You can go home.

262
00:21:43,505 --> 00:21:45,225
What about you, though?

263
00:21:45,825 --> 00:21:48,985
I've still got a bit of work left.
I'll probably finish late.

264
00:21:50,225 --> 00:21:54,065
I'll get going now, then.
Get home safe, Ms. Neen.

265
00:21:54,145 --> 00:21:55,585
Alright. Thank you.

266
00:23:29,905 --> 00:23:30,985
Hello?

267
00:23:31,065 --> 00:23:32,585
<i>I have your daughter.</i>

268
00:23:34,505 --> 00:23:36,665
Who are you? What are you talking about?

269
00:23:36,745 --> 00:23:39,065
If you want your daughter back safely,

270
00:23:39,145 --> 00:23:40,865
do as I say!

271
00:23:40,945 --> 00:23:42,065
Neen!

272
00:23:42,585 --> 00:23:44,305
Mom, let me talk to them.

273
00:23:44,985 --> 00:23:45,825
What's going on?

274
00:23:49,225 --> 00:23:51,105
Hello. Who are you?

275
00:23:51,185 --> 00:23:52,345
<i>Listen to me carefully.</i>

276
00:23:52,425 --> 00:23:54,345
Get me 30 million,

277
00:23:55,265 --> 00:23:56,625
<i>or your sister dies!</i>

278
00:23:56,705 --> 00:23:58,305
Don't joke like that.

279
00:23:58,385 --> 00:24:01,025
No more prank calls,
or I'm telling the police.

280
00:24:08,065 --> 00:24:09,745
Did he kidnap Neen?

281
00:24:10,745 --> 00:24:14,225
I don't think so. I'll try calling her.

282
00:24:14,305 --> 00:24:16,105
Yeah, call her.

283
00:24:20,745 --> 00:24:22,545
Hello. Neen? Where are you?

284
00:24:30,585 --> 00:24:34,745
On my rounds, I found this bag
and this car key right here on the floor.

285
00:24:52,785 --> 00:24:53,705
Dad.

286
00:24:55,625 --> 00:24:57,345
Go ahead and call the police.

287
00:24:59,905 --> 00:25:03,425
What's going on? Did they find Neen?

288
00:25:04,425 --> 00:25:07,945
That call earlier was real.

289
00:25:08,545 --> 00:25:09,745
What?

290
00:25:10,585 --> 00:25:11,585
Neen…

291
00:25:20,985 --> 00:25:23,505
-Hello?
-Why the hell did you hang up?

292
00:25:23,585 --> 00:25:25,025
You want your daughter to die?

293
00:25:25,105 --> 00:25:26,705
Calm down, okay?

294
00:25:26,785 --> 00:25:28,225
Tell me what you need.

295
00:25:28,305 --> 00:25:30,025
<i>I already told you.</i>

296
00:25:30,105 --> 00:25:32,225
I need 30 million.

297
00:25:32,825 --> 00:25:34,545
But if you tell the police,

298
00:25:35,105 --> 00:25:36,785
you'll get her back in pieces.

299
00:25:39,625 --> 00:25:42,985
How can we be sure she's really safe?

300
00:25:45,065 --> 00:25:46,905
You guys sure ask for a lot.

301
00:25:52,785 --> 00:25:55,065
Wake up. Wake up!

302
00:25:57,945 --> 00:25:59,105
Who are you?

303
00:25:59,865 --> 00:26:00,865
Where am I?

304
00:26:00,945 --> 00:26:02,585
Why'd you kidnap me?

305
00:26:03,265 --> 00:26:04,025
Shut up!

306
00:26:06,185 --> 00:26:09,225
Tell your parents you're okay.

307
00:26:10,705 --> 00:26:13,105
Dad, Mom, help!

308
00:26:13,185 --> 00:26:15,265
-Neen!
-Neen!

309
00:26:18,465 --> 00:26:20,865
Happy now? She's still breathing.

310
00:26:20,945 --> 00:26:24,585
But you decide how long
she stays that way.

311
00:26:25,785 --> 00:26:29,545
Okay, okay. Where should
we bring the money?

312
00:26:29,625 --> 00:26:32,545
I'll tell you that later. And remember,

313
00:26:32,625 --> 00:26:33,785
don't try anything smart.

314
00:26:36,105 --> 00:26:39,385
What should we do now?

315
00:26:39,465 --> 00:26:40,505
What should we do?

316
00:26:42,345 --> 00:26:43,225
&lrm;It's okay.

317
00:26:54,345 --> 00:26:57,465
We checked the CCTV cameras
near the office

318
00:26:57,545 --> 00:27:00,345
and found the suspect leaving the lot
onto a back road.

319
00:27:00,425 --> 00:27:02,585
The road is on a district border,

320
00:27:02,665 --> 00:27:04,905
so no BMA cameras are installed there,

321
00:27:04,985 --> 00:27:07,745
and the local private ones
have blind spots.

322
00:27:08,345 --> 00:27:11,585
So we have no idea where he took Neen?

323
00:27:11,665 --> 00:27:15,305
Right now, we can't track
his escape route past that point.

324
00:27:17,265 --> 00:27:18,945
So how will we track him down?

325
00:27:19,025 --> 00:27:21,145
We're following other leads instead,

326
00:27:21,225 --> 00:27:22,745
like phone signals,

327
00:27:22,825 --> 00:27:26,545
driving patterns, and suspects involved.

328
00:27:32,185 --> 00:27:33,785
What should we do, honey?

329
00:27:35,785 --> 00:27:37,265
They're taking forever.

330
00:27:39,985 --> 00:27:41,545
I need to use the restroom.

331
00:27:43,385 --> 00:27:45,585
What now? Don't try anything funny.

332
00:27:45,665 --> 00:27:48,785
I'm not. I really need
to use the restroom.

333
00:27:49,305 --> 00:27:50,705
I wouldn't dare run away.

334
00:27:53,505 --> 00:27:54,905
You sure ask for a lot.

335
00:28:25,225 --> 00:28:26,225
Hello?

336
00:28:26,305 --> 00:28:29,265
Hello. Runch, help me! Utt kidnapped me!

337
00:28:29,345 --> 00:28:32,625
Neen? Where are you?

338
00:28:34,145 --> 00:28:35,785
I don't know! I have zero clue.

339
00:28:35,865 --> 00:28:38,505
Calm down, okay? Send me your location.

340
00:28:38,585 --> 00:28:42,105
Find a place to hide now.
I'll get there as soon as I can.

341
00:28:55,905 --> 00:28:58,185
NEW MESSAGE

342
00:29:07,385 --> 00:29:08,665
6 KILOMETERS

343
00:29:17,225 --> 00:29:18,505
Hello, Runch?

344
00:29:20,465 --> 00:29:22,025
Neen called you?

345
00:29:26,145 --> 00:29:27,145
Okay.

346
00:29:29,385 --> 00:29:30,545
Neen called Runch.

347
00:29:35,625 --> 00:29:36,665
Peeracha!

348
00:29:38,105 --> 00:29:41,265
Come out! You really think
you could run away?

349
00:29:42,185 --> 00:29:43,265
Peeracha!

350
00:29:46,345 --> 00:29:47,425
Come out!

351
00:29:50,185 --> 00:29:51,425
Shit.

352
00:29:52,585 --> 00:29:53,785
Come out!

353
00:30:44,185 --> 00:30:45,145
Damn it!

354
00:31:02,785 --> 00:31:03,665
Runch!

355
00:31:05,145 --> 00:31:07,265
I'm here now. Don't be afraid.

356
00:31:17,945 --> 00:31:19,185
Don't be afraid.

357
00:31:19,705 --> 00:31:20,785
I'm here now.

358
00:31:24,745 --> 00:31:25,985
Good that you're both here.

359
00:31:28,865 --> 00:31:30,345
This way, I can kill you both.

360
00:31:51,705 --> 00:31:54,025
Freeze! Put your hands up!

361
00:31:54,825 --> 00:31:55,945
Put them up!

362
00:31:58,385 --> 00:31:59,505
Put them up!

363
00:32:09,505 --> 00:32:12,265
Neen. Neen!

364
00:32:18,065 --> 00:32:20,745
You're safe now, honey. You're home now.

365
00:32:25,745 --> 00:32:27,465
Go upstairs and get some rest, honey.

366
00:32:45,465 --> 00:32:48,385
Thank you for saving Neen, Runch.

367
00:32:50,785 --> 00:32:52,465
Also,

368
00:32:52,985 --> 00:32:55,305
there was something else
I wanted to tell you.

369
00:32:58,705 --> 00:33:00,425
The police called me.

370
00:33:03,105 --> 00:33:07,025
They said Utt named Mrs. Gingkamol
for giving the order.

371
00:33:11,145 --> 00:33:13,705
They'll call her in for questioning.

372
00:33:16,305 --> 00:33:18,305
I figured you'd want to hear this.

373
00:33:28,385 --> 00:33:29,505
Yes.

374
00:33:33,785 --> 00:33:37,065
Thank you for letting me know.

375
00:33:37,665 --> 00:33:39,785
But I'd rather stay out of it

376
00:33:40,385 --> 00:33:42,505
and let the law take its course.

377
00:33:45,465 --> 00:33:46,745
You reap

378
00:33:47,425 --> 00:33:50,025
what you sow.

379
00:33:55,145 --> 00:33:56,465
Come in.

380
00:34:04,465 --> 00:34:08,385
I'm here as Mrs. Gingkamol's lawyer.

381
00:34:10,025 --> 00:34:11,545
Please have a seat.

382
00:34:16,945 --> 00:34:20,025
For Mrs. Gingkamol's case, it turns out

383
00:34:20,105 --> 00:34:25,025
the investigators can't charge her
with solicitation of kidnapping.

384
00:34:26,465 --> 00:34:28,545
Utt did name her,

385
00:34:28,625 --> 00:34:30,905
but there's no evidence.

386
00:34:30,985 --> 00:34:33,865
No recordings, messages,

387
00:34:33,945 --> 00:34:35,225
or money transfers.

388
00:34:35,824 --> 00:34:37,665
There's nothing to confirm

389
00:34:37,744 --> 00:34:39,705
that she was the mastermind.

390
00:34:40,505 --> 00:34:44,225
So legally, she can't be charged.

391
00:34:45,025 --> 00:34:46,385
So my mom's off the hook.

392
00:34:48,744 --> 00:34:49,744
Yes.

393
00:34:52,105 --> 00:34:54,784
I knew this would happen.

394
00:34:55,865 --> 00:34:57,585
Are you disappointed?

395
00:34:58,705 --> 00:34:59,665
Yes.

396
00:35:00,905 --> 00:35:02,225
And angry.

397
00:35:02,825 --> 00:35:05,065
Not with the law,

398
00:35:06,225 --> 00:35:09,185
but the fact that
some people can hurt others

399
00:35:10,065 --> 00:35:12,105
without any consequences.

400
00:35:15,665 --> 00:35:16,985
I understand.

401
00:35:18,025 --> 00:35:20,785
Actually, she wanted to speak with you.

402
00:35:21,305 --> 00:35:24,265
She said she wanted to explain
and clear the air.

403
00:35:25,745 --> 00:35:27,145
No need for that.

404
00:35:27,745 --> 00:35:30,465
No explanation can undo
what really happened.

405
00:35:32,145 --> 00:35:34,025
Just because she wasn't charged

406
00:35:34,745 --> 00:35:36,265
doesn't mean she isn't guilty.

407
00:35:43,025 --> 00:35:45,065
MOM

408
00:35:54,585 --> 00:35:57,945
Why won't she pick up? It's been days!

409
00:35:59,585 --> 00:36:00,425
Honey, look.

410
00:36:00,505 --> 00:36:03,545
Runch has been ignoring my calls for days.
What's going on?

411
00:36:03,625 --> 00:36:06,425
Do you really not know
why she's like that?

412
00:36:06,505 --> 00:36:08,985
What's that supposed to mean?
I didn't do anything wrong.

413
00:36:09,065 --> 00:36:11,425
Can't you see?
Even the police can't arrest me.

414
00:36:12,065 --> 00:36:15,265
Sure, you weren't charged with anything.

415
00:36:15,865 --> 00:36:17,905
Exactly. So I'm not guilty.

416
00:36:17,985 --> 00:36:21,105
But you know full well what the truth is.

417
00:36:22,345 --> 00:36:23,585
What are you implying?

418
00:36:24,385 --> 00:36:26,665
I'm not guilty. Don't accuse me.

419
00:36:26,745 --> 00:36:28,665
I'm not accusing you.

420
00:36:28,745 --> 00:36:30,985
I just choose not to lie to myself,
unlike you.

421
00:36:31,065 --> 00:36:32,865
You want me to go to jail that bad?

422
00:36:32,945 --> 00:36:36,025
Yes. If it will set you straight.

423
00:36:36,105 --> 00:36:39,625
At least it will stop you
from hurting others,

424
00:36:39,705 --> 00:36:40,785
especially our daughter!

425
00:36:40,865 --> 00:36:42,785
-But I--
-Enough!

426
00:36:44,105 --> 00:36:45,865
Stop bothering Runch.

427
00:36:46,385 --> 00:36:48,465
She's suffered enough already.

428
00:37:02,225 --> 00:37:04,905
No. I did nothing wrong.

429
00:37:05,785 --> 00:37:06,985
Absolutely not.

430
00:37:24,825 --> 00:37:26,665
Gingkamol's off the hook?

431
00:37:31,745 --> 00:37:32,705
Really?

432
00:37:33,505 --> 00:37:34,865
That's not fair at all, Dad.

433
00:37:34,945 --> 00:37:36,305
What she did was serious.

434
00:37:36,385 --> 00:37:38,025
She had someone kidnapped for ransom,

435
00:37:38,105 --> 00:37:39,585
yet she's off the hook?

436
00:37:39,665 --> 00:37:41,145
Wouldn't that encourage her?

437
00:37:45,225 --> 00:37:47,585
Can't we do anything to someone like her?

438
00:37:51,905 --> 00:37:54,385
If the law can't punish someone like her,

439
00:37:55,585 --> 00:37:57,425
then we'll leave it to karma.

440
00:37:57,505 --> 00:37:59,385
Sooner or later,

441
00:37:59,985 --> 00:38:02,545
she'll get her karma
for what she did to us.

442
00:38:14,665 --> 00:38:16,065
Ungrateful daughter.

443
00:38:30,905 --> 00:38:31,785
Hello?

444
00:38:31,865 --> 00:38:33,905
<i>Hello, Mrs. Gingkamol.</i>

445
00:38:33,985 --> 00:38:36,305
<i>I'm calling from</i>
<i>the VIP Customer Care team</i>

446
00:38:36,385 --> 00:38:39,065
<i>at the bank where you hold</i>
<i>your fixed deposit account.</i>

447
00:38:39,865 --> 00:38:41,145
<i>Is everything alright?</i>

448
00:38:41,225 --> 00:38:43,905
<i>I have a quick special offer</i>
<i>I'd love to share.</i>

449
00:38:43,985 --> 00:38:48,305
<i>We have a new investment product</i>
<i>that offers returns several times higher</i>

450
00:38:48,385 --> 00:38:50,985
<i>than what you're earning</i>
<i>on your fixed deposit interest.</i>

451
00:38:51,065 --> 00:38:55,865
<i>If you're interested, your money can grow</i>
<i>significantly in just a few months</i>

452
00:38:55,945 --> 00:38:59,465
<i>without the risks of the stock market,</i>
<i>and it's completely hassle-free.</i>

453
00:39:00,585 --> 00:39:02,825
-Sounds too good to be true.
<i>-But,</i>

454
00:39:02,905 --> 00:39:07,145
I can assure you, this offer
is reserved for our VIP customers,

455
00:39:07,225 --> 00:39:09,985
<i>and you're the first person</i>
<i>I chose to call.</i>

456
00:39:10,065 --> 00:39:11,545
What will I have to do?

457
00:39:12,145 --> 00:39:15,745
<i>It's very simple, actually.</i>
<i>I'll message you the details.</i>

458
00:39:15,825 --> 00:39:19,385
<i>You'll just have to verify your identity</i>
<i>and transfer the money from your account</i>

459
00:39:19,465 --> 00:39:21,385
<i>to an investment account.</i>

460
00:39:22,065 --> 00:39:24,665
In that case, please send me the details.

461
00:39:25,345 --> 00:39:27,625
DIVORCE AGREEMENT

462
00:39:27,705 --> 00:39:29,865
SIGNATURE - RUNCHLAPHAT TRIKITTIPHUM
SIGNATURE - PEERACHA PACHARATHAKUL

463
00:39:41,825 --> 00:39:43,385
Still undecided?

464
00:39:47,705 --> 00:39:49,385
This isn't easy at all, Dad.

465
00:39:51,425 --> 00:39:53,865
I don't mean to rush your decision.

466
00:39:55,025 --> 00:39:56,705
I just want you

467
00:39:57,345 --> 00:39:59,025
to listen to your heart.

468
00:40:02,705 --> 00:40:04,465
Will you really be fine

469
00:40:05,745 --> 00:40:07,785
with having to be extra careful,

470
00:40:08,745 --> 00:40:11,745
never knowing when
someone will hurt you again?

471
00:40:14,585 --> 00:40:16,985
I'm not mad at Runch, though.

472
00:40:19,705 --> 00:40:21,105
I'm sure

473
00:40:22,185 --> 00:40:24,305
she's just as hurt as I am.

474
00:40:28,305 --> 00:40:29,345
I know.

475
00:40:30,425 --> 00:40:32,105
I'm not mad at her either.

476
00:40:36,625 --> 00:40:37,945
But I'm your father.

477
00:40:40,545 --> 00:40:43,745
I can't stand seeing my daughter
get hurt anymore,

478
00:40:45,425 --> 00:40:47,985
whether it's intentional or not.

479
00:41:05,385 --> 00:41:06,705
BOTH OF THE SPOUSES HAVE READ
AND UNDERSTOOD ALL OF THE ABOVE CONDITIONS

480
00:41:14,385 --> 00:41:16,465
SIGNATURE
RUNCHLAPHAT TRIKITTIPHUM - SPOUSE 1

481
00:41:16,545 --> 00:41:18,545
SIGNATURE
PEERACHA PACHARATHAKUL - SPOUSE 2

482
00:41:31,585 --> 00:41:33,105
MARRIAGE CERTIFICATE - THIS CERTIFIES THAT

483
00:41:33,185 --> 00:41:35,545
MISS RUNCHLAPHAT AND MISS PEERACHA
HAVE REGISTERED THEIR MARRIAGE

484
00:41:51,065 --> 00:41:52,665
Guess it's time now.

485
00:42:20,145 --> 00:42:23,025
LAST YEAR

486
00:42:29,345 --> 00:42:30,505
Neen!

487
00:42:31,545 --> 00:42:32,465
Neen.

488
00:42:34,265 --> 00:42:35,105
&lrm;Let me see.

489
00:42:36,785 --> 00:42:37,985
Come on.

490
00:42:38,705 --> 00:42:40,385
Let's get you patched up.

491
00:42:57,465 --> 00:42:59,105
I'll clean it up for you.

492
00:43:09,625 --> 00:43:11,705
This might sting a bit.

493
00:43:13,225 --> 00:43:16,905
Seeing you hurt hurts me more.

494
00:43:24,465 --> 00:43:25,545
Can you blow on it?

495
00:43:35,465 --> 00:43:36,825
All done.

496
00:43:41,945 --> 00:43:43,065
&lrm;Come on.

497
00:43:58,705 --> 00:44:00,265
All done now?

498
00:44:00,345 --> 00:44:02,865
Almost. Here.

499
00:44:03,385 --> 00:44:04,945
The last step.

500
00:44:29,345 --> 00:44:31,425
If something were to happen to you,

501
00:44:32,705 --> 00:44:34,745
I wouldn't be able to go on.

502
00:44:52,425 --> 00:44:54,025
This is where we started,

503
00:44:54,105 --> 00:44:55,625
so I wanted us to end things here.

504
00:44:55,705 --> 00:44:57,625
No matter what our relationship is,

505
00:44:57,705 --> 00:45:00,745
you're the best thing in my life.

506
00:45:00,825 --> 00:45:02,505
<i>Same here.</i>

507
00:45:08,185 --> 00:45:11,465
I never imagined
I'd get to be here either.

508
00:45:12,065 --> 00:45:15,545
Who knows? You might
get back together with Neen

509
00:45:15,625 --> 00:45:17,305
and end up remarrying.

510
00:45:17,385 --> 00:45:21,185
If that ever happens… that'd be great.

511
00:46:05,385 --> 00:46:07,825
Subtitle translation by:
Ramil Natnitiwitaya

